course: dictionary
lesson: 13197
title: Fulfilled: promises kept and dreams come true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fulfilled comes from the verb fulfil, which means to do what you promised or to carry out what was needed. The past form is fulfilled. «Mia promised to finish her model ship, and on Friday she had fulfilled her promise.» The promise was kept, so it was fulfilled.
explain: Fulfilled can also describe a dream or hope that has come true. «Sam had wanted a puppy for years, and when he finally got one, his dream was fulfilled.» Look at the clues: wanted for years, finally got one. They tell you the dream became real.
explain: As an adjective, fulfilled describes a feeling. «Mrs Patel felt fulfilled after a year of helping her class learn to read.» A fulfilled person is happy and satisfied because their life or work feels meaningful. Ask yourself: is this about a promise, a dream or a feeling? The context tells you which.
fact: Fulfil is the base verb. Fulfilled is its past form, and it can also be an adjective.
fact: «Fulfilled» can mean done as promised, as in «a promise fulfilled».
fact: «Fulfilled» can mean come true, as in «a dream fulfilled».
fact: As an adjective, «fulfilled» means happy and satisfied because your life or work feels meaningful.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in kept, come true or satisfied. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Tom promised to clean the pond, and by Sunday his promise was fulfilled.» What does fulfilled mean here? | Painted bright blue | *Done as promised | Cancelled by the rain | Forgotten and left undone
exercise: «Ava had dreamed of seeing the sea for years, and at last her dream was fulfilled.» What does fulfilled mean here? | Put away in a box | Broken into pieces | Lost at sea | *Came true
exercise: «After years of teaching, Mr Ahmed felt fulfilled.» What does fulfilled suggest about how he feels? | *Happy and satisfied with his work | Angry with his class | Tired of school | Lonely and bored
test: «The village was promised a new well, and the promise was fulfilled when it was built.» What does fulfilled mean here? | Painted white | Hidden under the ground | *Done as promised | Argued about
test: Which sentence uses fulfilled to show deep satisfaction? | The rain fulfilled all afternoon | The bread was fulfilled in the oven | *Sara felt fulfilled after years of caring for sick animals | Tim fulfilled his bike with a pump
exam: Which word means the same as fulfilled when a dream comes true? | Forgotten | Frozen | Stolen | *Realised
